# Security Rules

- Never log credentials, tokens, private keys, or secret values.
- Prefer workload identity/OIDC/federated identity over long-lived static credentials.
- Treat cross-namespace secret/credential references as privilege-sensitive.
- Use least-privilege RBAC.
- Separate controller identity from workload identity when possible.
- Admission-time safety checks should reject known-dangerous configurations rather than relying only on reconciliation.
- Supply-chain output should eventually include SBOM, signatures, and provenance for public releases.
- Third-party ReconcileBench findings require responsible disclosure before public publication.
- Do not create hidden backdoors or test-only bypasses in release builds.
- Destructive cloud actions require explicit lifecycle/deletion semantics and tests.
